<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cornelis Speelman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1628–1684</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cornelis Speelman was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> commander and governor-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a> from 1681 to 1684. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arung-palakka">Arung Palakka</a> of Bone, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-hasanuddin">Sultan Hasanuddin</a> of Gowa and imposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bongaya">Treaty of Bongaya</a> of 1667, which ended Makassar's power and its free trade. He later campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trunajaya">Trunajaya</a>'s rebellion on behalf of the Mataram court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cornelis-speelman.jpg" alt="Cornelis Speelman" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Martin Palin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Cornelis_Speelman_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
